@page "/"

<PageTitle>IntentBlazor — AI application framework</PageTitle>

<p class="eyebrow">OPEN SOURCE · MIT LICENSED</p>
<h1>User intent.<br />A living interface.</h1>
<p class="lead">An AI-centric Blazor framework built around two interaction components.
    Connect your model, expose your C# capabilities, and let the workspace take shape around the task.</p>
<p class="status"><strong>Phase 4 content and extension tools implemented.</strong> Attach files, inspect dynamic previews,
    and create an actual resized image in the content demo. Live model verification remains deferred.</p>
<div class="actions">
    <a class="button" href="/playground">Try the playground</a>
    <a class="button secondary" href="/workspaces">Try draft recovery</a>
    <a class="button secondary" href="/content">Try content and extensions</a>
</div>

<section class="card-grid" aria-label="Framework direction">
    <article class="card">
        <p class="eyebrow">INPUT</p>
        <h2>Express the task</h2>
        <p>AiInput sends text and workspace context to a registered processor. The optional content package adds bounded file attachments.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
        <p class="eyebrow">OUTPUT</p>
        <h2>Work with the result</h2>
        <p>AiOutput composes validated interactive views, preserves direct edits, and executes explicitly registered server actions.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
        <p class="eyebrow">DEVELOPER EXPERIENCE</p>
        <h2>Bring your application</h2>
        <p>Expose C# data tools, register typed renderer packs, and embed optional AI setup/inspection. You own identity, permissions, and business rules.</p>
    </article>
</section>

<section>
    <h2>Three applications to prove the foundation</h2>
    <p>Gaming News and Tips explores content and sources. Staff Business exercises permissions and shared records.
        Asset Workbench explores previews, edits, and generated artifacts.</p>
    <p>The playground already uses the same document, state, binding, and interaction mechanisms for all three fixture workspaces.
        The recovery demo adds private SQLite checkpoints and shared synthetic staff records. Complete standalone workflows follow in Phase 5.</p>
</section>
